# Platform layer — infra only

`backend/src/platform/` is process and shared infrastructure. It is **not** a home for
product behavior.

## Allowed in `platform/`

Env/config loading, error catalog, Mongo connection, logger, secret crypto, shutdown,
base schema helpers, idempotency.

## Forbidden in `platform/`

Context budgeter, tokenizer/compaction, LLM client, LangGraph, agent tools, ingest,
identity/RBAC use cases, knowledge assembly, conversation prompt logic.

## Where domain code goes

The four modules only: `access`, `masters`, `knowledge`, `conversation`. Cross-module
callers import that module’s public `index.js`.

```js
// ❌ BAD — conversation math dumped into platform
// backend/src/platform/context/contextBudgeter.js

// ✅ GOOD — conversation owns context accounting
// backend/src/modules/conversation/contextBudgeter.js
```

Do not add `platform/context/` or `platform/llm/`. See `node-api.mdc`.
